Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer
exclusive Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) upon the creator
and subsequent owner(s) (each and all, an "owner") of an original work of
authorship and/or a database (each, a "Work").

Certain owners wish to permanently relinquish those rights to a Work for
the purpose of contributing to a commons of creative, cultural and
scientific works that the public can reliably and without fear of later
claims of infringement build upon, modify, incorporate in other works, reuse
and retain, and redistribute as freely as possible in any form whatsoever
and for any purpose, including commercial purposes. These owners may wish
to contribute to the commons to promote the progress of science, culture,
and the creation of useful new works. For these and/or other purposes and
motivations, and without any expectation of additional consideration or
compensation, the person associating CC0 with a Work (the "Affirmer") to the
following terms and conditions has granted to the public, at no charge, a
worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, irrevocable copyright license to
reproduce, adapt, distribute, perform, display, communicate, and otherwise
use the Work for any purpose, and to make Derivative Works that are based
upon, incorporate in, or derived from the Work, as long as the copyright
notice in the Work is not removed or changed. The following rights are not
affected by the above and are retained by the owner of the Work if the Work
contains copyright notices and otherwise is not in the public domain.

The above rights are not necessarily all of the rights granted by the
copyright owner. The following rights are not affected by the above:

  1. Rights of other persons or organizations, whether or not the Work is
     itself a copyrighted work, in the Work or in how the Work is used,
     such as publicity or privacy rights.
  2. Moral rights retained by the author, including the right to be
     identified as the author of the Work, where reasonable.
  3. Copyright or neighboring rights in any code or other elements in the
     Work that are not part of the Work, such as technology, software, and
     symbols, and any associated documentation or manuals.

The Work is provided "AS IS" and the Affirmer makes no representations or
warranties of any kind concerning the Work, express, implied, statutory or
otherwise, including without limitation warranties of title,
merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, non infringement, or the
absence of latent or other defects, accuracy, or the presence of errors,
whether or not discoverable, and to the extent permitted by applicable law,
no implied warranties are disclaimed.

The Affirmer disclaims responsibility for clearing rights of other persons
that may apply to the Work or any use thereof, including without limitation
